# The backend deployment only needs the Python modules at the repository root.
# Both frontends are separate Vercel projects and must not be bundled into the
# function, and the data directories would blow past the bundle size for no
# reason — sensor data is read from the bucket at runtime, never from the image.

frontend/
frontend-participant/
node_modules/

data/
plots/
reports/
newplot/
tests/
1/

*.csv
*.avro
*.parquet
*.ipynb

__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Never bundle the participant roster into a deployment. It holds login
# PINs and reaches the deployed API through PARTICIPANT_CONFIG_JSON.
# Excluding it means a missing env var fails loudly at boot rather than
# silently shipping PINs inside the function.
participant_config.json
